endation, reference discussion, give evidence, implication.\n\nWe should decide vote. Let's evaluate: Candidate A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: sometimes not good at taking criticism, eats unhealthily. Also from Agent 1 notes: unfriendly, show\u2011off demeanor. No evidence on stress resilience, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, adaptability. So many unknowns.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, can be grumpy, sometimes adopts wrong tone. No info on crew cooperation, decision quality, technical competence beyond weather/computer, attention.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, known to be 100% reliable, excellent attention skills. Also from Agent 1: keeps calm in crisis, puts concern for others above everything. So strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, crew cooperation, reliability, attention. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, unwillingness to further education (adaptability). Overall strong.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, regarded as a loner. Strengths: responsibility, concentration, problem solving. Concerns: arrogance, loner (crew cooperation), maybe temperament.\n\nThus Candidate C seems strongest across many criteria, despite communication concerns. Candidate B has stress resilience and conscientiousness but lacks crew cooperation and decision quality evidence. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but unknown stress and crew cooperation. Candidate D has responsibility but poor crew cooperation.\n\nThus I think Candidate C is best overall. So we should align with Agent 1 and vote Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's recommendation and explain why we think C is better. Provide evidence: decision quality, stress resilience, crew cooperation, reliability, attention. Mention concerns but argue they are less critical or can be mitigated.\n\nThus public message: I disagree with Agent 3, I recommend Candidate C. Provide evidence.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
